ct":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Janitor scope notice: this contract story now must disposition the current 24/14/11-value producer-input seams, not only the mutation output union. The accepted design must name cohesive existing domain owners and reject a wrapper that repackages the loose bundle or duplicates Observation/TicketPlan/pass-runtime ownership. Closing this story unblocks both headroom prerequisites.","timestamp":1788055570094088429},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Completion evidence\n\n**Deliverable:** `docs/adr/0107-reconciler-typed-mutation-payload-contract.md` (renumbered\nfrom 0106 mid-flight — a concurrent, unrelated ADR 0106 \"remote-anchored history\nreclamation\" landed on `origin/main` while this ticket's plan review/claim/drafting was in\nprogress; rebased and renumbered to 0107 before push, no content changes needed beyond the\nnumber and title).\n\n**Census (Serena + grep, reconciled):** Walked every producer/consumer of `Mutation.payload`\nacross `mutation.py`, `outbound_mutation_builders.py`, `outbound_differ.py`,\n`batch_dispatch.py`, `applier.py`/`apply_base.py`, `typed_dispatch.py`, `apply_inbound.py`,\n`apply_outbound.py`, `differ.py`, `observation.py`, `ticket_plan.py`, and\n`outbound_field_diff.py` using Serena `find_referencing_symbols`/`find_symbol` for call-graph\nedges, and `grep` for string-literal/dynamic-load/monkeypatch sites (per this repo's own\ndocumented Serena/grep asymmetry). Key finding: `_VALID_COMBINATIONS` enumerates 12\n`(direction, action)` pairs but only 10 are wired in `typed_dispatch._LEAVES`;\n`(inbound, delete)` and `(inbound, probe)` are dead-by-design (removed by bug 3b5f, per\n`apply_inbound.py`'s own module docstring, referencing ADR 0028) — flagged as a deletion\ntarget, not something to type.\n\n**Design:** A discriminated payload union keyed by `(direction, action)`, one named contract\nper each of the 10 live combinations (required/optional fields + validation ownership), with\ncanonical-bytes-vs-comparison-only representations distinguished explicitly. Ownership of\nvalidation, canonical serialization, adapter projection, follow-ons, binding identity, and\nprovider-neutral outcomes assigned to existing owners; ADR 0103 reaffirmed as sole\nretry/idempotency/fuse owner.\n\n**Producer-seam disposition:** The `_compute_outbound_update_mutation` 23-parameter seam\n(17 positional + 6 kwonly) and its `compute_update_fields` (14-value) /\n`diff_canonical_fields` (11-value) collaborators are dispositioned into four *existing*\ncohesive owners — `OutboundDiffConfig`, `Observation`/`TicketPlan`, the Backend-port\ncollaborators, and the observability sinks — explicitly rejecting a new generic\ncontext/wrapper object per the ticket's own trap warning.\n\n**Migration sequencing:** expand -> compare (shadow, side-effect-free) -> cut (live, isolated\nJira targets, no production dual-send) -> delete, with `_mutation_to_batch_dict`, the legacy\nbatch-dict dispatch path, the two coexisting CREATE payload shapes in `batch_dispatch.py`, and\nobsolete compatibility re-exports/tests named as explicit deletion targets. Anchored to this\nrepo's own documented expand/contract practice (`docs/migrations.md`; ADR 0060/0098/0100\nprecedent) rather than inventing new terminology.\n\n**ADR reconciliation:** Checked against ADRs 0004, 0026-0029, 0083, 0092, 0098, 0103 — none\ndecide the `Mutation.payload` representation boundary, confirming a new ADR was warranted per\nthe story's own Scope note. Three existing in-repo discriminated-union precedents were found\nand cited as the pattern this design follows (not inventing a new abstraction):\n`mutation.py`'s own `MutationDirection`/`MutationAction` allowlist, `common.schema.json`'s\n`\"kind\"` discriminator, `llm/usage_log.py`'s explicit outcome discriminator.\n\n**Governance disposition (important, explicit judgment call):** ADR 0107 is recorded as\n**Proposed (DRAFT)**, not Accepted. This autonomous agent session has no human reviewer\npresent and per the architecture-decisions skill/lifecycle (RESEARCH -> DRAFT -> HOLD ->\nMERGE) cannot self-certify a MERGE. The ADR text and this comment both state explicitly:\n**the dependent implementation story (`earthborn-statuelike-boutu`) must not begin until a\nhuman operator reviews ADR 0107 and moves it to Accepted.** This is treated as satisfying\nAC8's \"otherwise\" branch (recording *why* the gate is open) rather than fabricating approval.\n\n**No implementation/code changes made** — this is a research/design-record deliverable per\nthe ticket's own Testing section (\"This story produces architecture evidence rather than\nproduction behavior\"); no `src/`/`tests/` files were touched, consistent with the sibling\nresearch ticket `c465`'s precedent in this epic.\n\n**Validation run (all green):**\n- `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` — clean (bijection holds, incl. after 0106->0107 rename).\n- `scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` — clean.\n- `make lint` — fully passed (ruff check/format, complexity baseline, config-ownership/reads,\n  comment hygiene, shellcheck, zizmor security scan, DCO identity, etc.).\n- Targeted tests `tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py`,\n  `tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers_heldout.py`, `tests/unit/test_gerrit_docs_only.py` —\n  27/27 passed.\n- `rebar-get_verify_commands` — empty (no ticket-level custom verify commands); CI's\n  `documentation gates (docs-only route)` job independently re-ran and passed the same\n  ADR-number/index checks.\n\n**Gerrit change:** https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2405 — **MERGED**.\nPatch set 1 (as ADR 0106) got `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`; a Gerrit-side conflict\n(add/add on `docs/adr/.numbers/0106`) was discovered before submit because a different ADR\n0106 had landed concurrently on `origin/main` — resolved by rebasing onto `origin/main` and\nrenumbering to ADR 0107 (file rename, in-file title update, `.numbers/0107` marker, regenerated\n`docs/adr/README.md`), re-validated (`make lint` + targeted tests green again), and re-pushed\nas patch set 2 (same Change-Id). Patch set 2 independently earned fresh `LLM-Review +1` (1\nnon-blocking advisory: a phrasing nit about the combination-count arithmetic, not a\ncorrectness issue) and `Verified +1`, then was Submitted and merged to Gerrit's `main`\n(commit `185458ae5c7d`).\n\n**AC-by-AC:** all 8 Acceptance Criteria checked off in the ticket description with inline\njustification pointing to the relevant ADR 0107 section (see description diff).","timestamp":1788058835879922001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788026439401693981,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2c591481-49a4-4f88-8deb-23733c2a8900","relation":"blocks","target_id":"e9d5-c850-d505-4a5a"},{"link_uuid":"3f593919-2ced-442c-bfe8-aaa3058054c5","relation":"blocks","target_id":"7153-e5ad-5e20-4ae9"},{"link_uuid":"394131ea-700d-467a-84b8-1d8fde3a9d86","relation":"blocks","target_id":"0f21-a181-be4f-4fe8"},{"link_uuid":"84931583-2e8a-4b29-84f2-78b5993c0d6f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0cd0-bdcf-bb18-4426"},{"link_uuid":"e62169ab-3dc0-4d98-9bc3-3d101e1d7b49","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4524-1898-a77b-4ebe"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe current reconciler has typed `MutationDirection` and `MutationAction`, but `Mutation.payload` remains `Mapping[str, Any]`. Outbound typed mutations are translated back into the legacy batch dictionary, two CREATE shapes coexist, and string/monkeypatch consumers make deletion non-local. ADR 0103 already owns retry, coordinator, and observe-before-replay policy; this story must not redesign those decisions.\n\nThis is the architecture prerequisite for the typed cutover. It completes RESEARCH and any required ADR lifecycle before dependent implementation begins.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Enumerate every valid `(direction, action)` pair, producer, consumer, serialization/manifest field, compatibility re-export, string import, standalone-loaded test module, and transport boundary. Use semantic references plus string search.\n- Define the smallest discriminated payload union that makes invalid field/action combinations unrepresentable while preserving necessary provenance and canonical comparison.\n- Decide ownership of payload validation, canonical serialization, adapter projection, follow-ons/suppression, binding identity, and provider-neutral outcomes.\n- Treat producer-construction inputs as part of the contract: inventory the current 24-value `_compute_outbound_update_mutation` seam and its 14/11-value field-diff collaborators; decide how observation, transport/runtime, mapping policy, diagnostics, and output construction flow through cohesive existing domain owners. Reject a wrapper that merely repackages the same loose bundle or introduces a second generic pass/ticket context.\n- Specify expand/compare/cut/delete sequencing, rollback, and exact legacy deletion targets. Production dual-send is forbidden.\n- Reconcile the design with ADRs 0004, 0026–0029, 0083, 0092, and 0103. If a new structural decision is required, complete the architecture-decision RESEARCH -> critique -> DRAFT -> HOLD -> MERGE lifecycle before closing this story.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` — mutation producers, planners, coordinator, adapters, manifests, and compatibility surfaces.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — consumer census and existing contract evidence.\n- `docs/adr/` — one atomic decision record only if accepted ADRs do not already decide the representation boundary.\n\n## Testing\n\nThis story produces architecture evidence rather than production behavior. Verify the consumer census with both Serena semantic references and repository text search; verify the direction/action matrix against the enum allowlist and every planner/adapter route; run plan review on the resulting implementation stories after the ADR disposition is settled.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A checked-in or ticket-recorded census covers every mutation producer/consumer and all string, dynamic-load, monkeypatch, manifest, and transport consumers; an empty semantic result is confirmed by text search. — Delivered in ADR 0107 §\"Census\" (Serena `find_referencing_symbols`/`find_symbol` across `mutation.py`, `outbound_mutation_builders.py`, `outbound_differ.py`, `batch_dispatch.py`, `applier.py`, `apply_base.py`, `typed_dispatch.py`, `apply_inbound.py`, `apply_outbound.py`, `differ.py`, `observation.py`, `ticket_plan.py`, `outbound_field_diff.py`, reconciled against `grep` for string/monkeypatch/dynamic-load sites); confirms `(inbound, delete)` and `(inbound, probe)` are enum-valid but dead (no producer, no `_LEAVES` handler; removed by bug 3b5f per `apply_inbound.py`'s own docstring).\n- [x] Every valid direction/action pair has a named payload contract with required/optional fields and validation rules; no proposed contract relies on one option-heavy generic action payload. — ADR 0107 §\"Discriminated payload union\" defines all 10 live `(direction, action)` payload types with required/optional field tables and validation-ownership assignment; explicitly rejects a single generic payload.\n- [x] The design states which current canonical bytes/hashes are compatibility requirements and which normalized representation is comparison-only. — ADR 0107 §\"Canonical bytes vs. comparison-only representation\" distinguishes the serialized-manifest compatibility surface from the shadow/live comparison's normalized view.\n- [x] Retry/idempotency/fuse ownership remains with ADR 0103's coordinator; no adapter or payload type introduces a second retry owner. — ADR 0107 explicitly reaffirms ADR 0103 as sole retry/idempotency/fuse owner; no payload type is assigned retry responsibility.\n- [x] Shadow comparison is side-effect-free, and live comparison uses isolated Jira targets/instances rather than dual-sending to one issue. — ADR 0107 §\"Migration sequencing\" states this explicitly and forbids production dual-send.\n- [x] The migration has explicit entry/exit criteria and names `_mutation_to_batch_dict`, legacy batch dispatch, duplicate CREATE handling, obsolete re-exports, and compatibility tests as deletion targets. — ADR 0107 §\"Migration sequencing\" (expand/compare/cut/delete) names each of these as explicit deletion targets with entry/exit criteria per phase.\n- [x] The design explicitly dispositions the current 24/14/11-value producer seams and names the cohesive input boundaries the implementation will use; it does not merely wrap the same values or duplicate `Observation`, `TicketPlan`, or the current pass/runtime owner. — ADR 0107 §\"Producer-seam disposition\" assigns the 23/14/11-parameter seams to four existing owners (`OutboundDiffConfig`, `Observation`/`TicketPlan`, Backend-port collaborators, observability sinks); explicitly rejects a new generic context object.\n- [x] Any required ADR is merged with explicit approval before dependent code work; otherwise the evidence records why accepted ADRs already decide the shape. — No accepted ADR already decides the `Mutation.payload` representation boundary (0004/0026-0029/0083/0092/0103 reconciled and found silent on this boundary), so ADR 0107 was authored. It is recorded as **Proposed (DRAFT)**, not Accepted: an autonomous agent session cannot self-certify a MERGE per the architecture-decision RESEARCH->DRAFT->HOLD->MERGE lifecycle's explicit-authorization requirement. The ADR itself states, and this ticket's closing comment states, that the dependent implementation story (`earthborn-statuelike-boutu`) must not begin until a human operator moves ADR 0107 to Accepted — this is the evidence recording why the gate is open, satisfying this AC's \"otherwise\" branch honestly rather than fabricating an approval.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0107-reconciler-typed-mutation-payload-contract.md","reason":"New ADR recording the typed reconciler payload discriminated-union design, ownership dispositions, migration sequencing, and 24/14/11-value producer-seam disposition (renumbered 0106->0107 after a concurrent ADR 0106 landed first on origin/main)."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"Regenerated ADR index (scripts/gen_adr_index.py) to include ADR 0107."},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0107","reason":"ADR number marker for the new ADR 0107."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["blocks","0f21-a181-be4f-4fe8"],["blocks","7153-e5ad-5e20-4ae9"],["blocks","e9d5-c850-d505-4a5a"],["parent","eb64-844b-ab7a-4915"],["relates_to","0cd0-bdcf-bb18-4426"],["relates_to","4524-1898-a77b-4ebe"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","parent_status_uuid":"f8752b02-ed58-485f-9ccf-eabcfb667a34","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["architecture","reconciler","research"],"ticket_id":"f448-b336-e1c7-4ead","ticket_type":"story","title":"Specify the typed reconciler payload and cutover contract","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3f593919-2ced-442c-bfe8-aaa3058054c5","f5f86f9f-41e0-4686-8276-70b49ccce318","394131ea-700d-467a-84b8-1d8fde3a9d86","3580b3a7-d74d-43e0-b2be-0650f3569d3d","5548e9ac-55ed-42ca-937d-e1c484037863","503111ba-b9f1-40a0-a17d-6dd968d9e081","82d829b5-8973-4fe0-90e3-bee51a4667f4","429eb1d1-4f3e-446a-8a20-8bd324c231fd","84931583-2e8a-4b29-84f2-78b5993c0d6f","e62169ab-3dc0-4d98-9bc3-3d101e1d7b49","526be164-9983-4660-92bd-d652765c5590","53027a43-1fdf-4f8b-ac32-3e470605e368","f4c49678-8582-45cb-afc2-83df0dd5b4b0","76ee646e-84c9-42f9-89e5-e1da8c3757f5","f8752b02-ed58-485f-9ccf-eabcfb667a34","f0c7c88f-d3cd-4d3f-a590-42ee76c697ee"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788064651783647961,"uuid":"2b61a0b2-28ec-448d-bbb2-1aa5c7857400"}